Bundled font provenance
=======================

Noto fonts
  Copyright 2012 Google Inc. All Rights Reserved.
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 - full text in LICENSE.Noto

  Desktop files: desktop/noto/ (8 files; 4,908,576 bytes)
  Web files: NotoSans-*.woff2 and NotoSansMono-*.woff2

Desktop font sources
  Acquired 2026-08-09. All files are registered privately at application
  startup and are never installed into the operating system.

  - Noto monthly release noto-monthly-release-2026.05.01, source commit
    66c4b351c58f99ace5a6265d329080d74b057909. The application retains the
    hinted static TTF Regular, Medium, SemiBold, and Bold faces for Noto Sans
    and Noto Sans Mono: 8 files and 4,908,576 bytes. These core families cover
    Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, IPA, combining marks, and common scientific
    punctuation.
    Source archive SHA-256:
    708d16915f7468f88d0dd9633ad25ce247561558122121dd78d8a664317f9e66

  Exact filenames and SHA-256 checksums for all 8 runtime files are in
  desktop/SHA256SUMS. The desktop payload is stored only under src/resources;
  it is not duplicated under docs/fonts/. Additional scripts and emoji use
  fonts installed by the user in the operating system.

Offline web-font source
  Acquired 2026-08-09 from Google Fonts CSS for Noto Sans weights 300-700
  and Noto Sans Mono weights 400-700. The returned variable WOFF2 files were
  saved locally and remote URLs were replaced by relative paths in fonts.css.
  The same compact 15-file, 757,252-byte set is copied under docs/fonts/ so
  the standalone documentation remains self-contained and offline.

